secubox-nac (3.1.0-1~bookworm1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Cross-plane Presence Guardian (#820, Project B) — stacked on the
    #817 Device Guardian consolidation.
  * New `presences`/`presence_alerts` tables (same `devices.db`, WAL) fed
    by four fail-safe, off-loop collectors: WAN (sbxwaf threat-log +
    User-Agent bot/crawler classification), LAN/WG (mirrors A's device
    store), and kbin (R3 toolbox tunnel `mac_hash` personas + report
    token deep-link).
  * Geo/provenance enrichment (`geo_cc`/`geo_asn`/`geo_org` for public
    IPs via the existing mmdb readers; `provenance` always set —
    geo/private/lan/tunnel/mesh/bot — even with no mmdb present).
  * Tiered alert engine (`api/presence/alerts.py`): WAN bot-surge,
    WAN new-country, and WG/LAN rogue-router (#817 risk_level=="high")
    checks; every fired condition is always recorded, while the EMAIL
    (sendmail, deduped/rate-limited per tier+plane+window) stays OFF
    until an operator supplies `/etc/secubox/presence-alerts.toml` — a
    commented `.example` ships under `/usr/share/secubox/nac/`, never
    the live path.
  * Scheduled presence report (`api/presence/reports.py`): a
    self-contained HTML/text report (per-plane counts, top geo/ASN,
    recent presences + alerts) plus `run_scheduled()`, wired to a new
    `secubox-presence-report.timer` (daily) → oneshot
    `secubox-presence-report.service` (`User=secubox`), and an
    on-demand `POST /presence/report/now`. The timer is enabled by
    default — it stays a harmless no-op until
    `/etc/secubox/reporter-schedule.json` is configured with a
    `frequency`+`recipient`.
  * New read-only `/presence`, `/presence/{id}`, `/presence/geo`,
    `/presence/alerts` (JWT-gated, plain `def`) and `POST
    /presence/sync` (forced collect) endpoints.
  * WebUI: new "Présence" cross-plane view (geo/provenance badges,
    tier-colored rows, geo/ASN aggregate panel, alerts panel, LAN/WG
    device deep-link, kbin report deep-link); all dynamic content via
    `E()`/`textContent`, no `innerHTML` of attacker-influenceable
    fields.
  * Tor collection and VLAN/Tor/mesh emancipation are explicitly NOT
    part of this release (deferred to Project C).

 -- Gerald KERMA <devel@cybermind.fr>  Sun, 05 Jul 2026 20:00:00 +0000

secubox-nac (3.0.0-1~bookworm1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Device Guardian consolidation (#817): secubox-nac becomes the single
    canonical Device Guardian, replacing secubox-mac-guard,
    secubox-device-intel and secubox-iot-guard.
  * New normalized SQLite device store (devices.db, WAL) with an
    idempotent legacy-store migration (mac-guard JSON, device-intel
    JSON, iot-guard SQLite) — MAC-canonical, per-column best-value
    merge, lossless.
  * One unified discovery pipeline (dnsmasq + ISC + ARP merge) replaces
    the four separate legacy pollers.
  * Absorbed enrichment: OUI vendor lookup (ieee-data), device-type /
    risk classification, OpenWrt/router fingerprinting.
  * Background collector + double-cache; all API handlers are now
    non-blocking plain `def` reading the cache/store — no inline
    discovery/scan work on the shared aggregator loop (#808).
  * mac-guard's whitelist/blacklist folded into nac's existing
    `allow_state` / `inet secubox_nac` zones (blocked / lan_allowed);
    its separate `inet secubox_mac_guard` nft sets are migrated into
    `secubox_nac` by a one-shot idempotent postinst step.
  * Absorbed endpoints: vendors, on-demand scan, OpenWrt LuCI probe,
    mDNS, device groups, JSON/CSV export.
  * WebUI: vendor/device-type/risk columns + fingerprint badges, groups
    view, CSV export.
  * secubox-mac-guard, secubox-device-intel and secubox-iot-guard now
    308-redirect their API surface to the nac equivalents (retained as
    thin compatibility shims); secubox-network-anomaly's previously
    open /status is now JWT-gated. Package removal is a separate gated
    follow-up, not part of this release.
  * Depends: add ieee-data (OUI vendor DB at /usr/share/ieee-data/oui.txt).

 -- Gerald KERMA <devel@cybermind.fr>  Sat, 05 Jul 2026 18:00:00 +0000

